{
  "abstract": "Formalizes Theorem 1.1 of Ideal Generation for General Reduced Projective Points. Over an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero, for every projective dimension n >= 1, degree D >= 2 and point count between binomial(n+D-1,D-1) and binomial(n+D,D)-1, a nonempty principal open of ordered reduced point configurations has maximal-rank multiplication from I_D tensor S_1 to I_(D+1). The homogeneous ideal has the exact predicted numbers of minimal generators in degrees D and D+1 and is generated in those degrees. Generality is expressed in the standard affine chart of projective space. The points are actual projective classes and their homogeneous ideal is radical.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Vlado Vojdanovski"
    }
  ],
